  "statement": "For a given positive composite integer N, consider all of its distinct prime factors. Let P_max be the largest prime factor of N, and P_min be the smallest prime factor of N.\n\nThe prime factor delta of N is defined as (P_max - P_min). If N is prime or 1, print 0 because there are not multiple distinct prime factors.",
  "inputFormat": "A single integer N.",
  "outputFormat": "Print the integer delta (P_max - P_min).",
  "constraints": "1 <= N <= 10^9",
  "sampleCases": [
    {
      "input": "12",
      "expectedOutput": "1",
      "explanation": "Prime factors of 12 are 2 and 3. Delta = 3 - 2 = 1."
    },
    {
      "input": "70",
      "expectedOutput": "5",
      "explanation": "Prime factors of 70 are 2, 5, 7. Delta = 7 - 2 = 5."
    },
    {
      "input": "13",
      "expectedOutput": "0",
      "explanation": "13 is prime, only one distinct factor."
    }
  ],
